    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d29-a1">

                <pb facs="0105" n="25" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg25"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowther to Mr.
                            Adee.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Newport, R.
                                I.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-09-01"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 1, 1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 240.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note No. 2223 of the
                    1st ultimo, I have the honor to transmit to you herewith a copy of a dispatch
                    addressed by His Majesty’s principal secretary of state for foreign affairs to
                    the United States minister at La Paz, thanking him for his good offices in
                    obtaining the release of George Melville, a British subject, lately imprisoned
                    at Corocoro, in Bolivia, on a charge of theft.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard Lowther.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
